 AT BY THEIR READER ALONE; 41 WAIT TO BE BUILT (register rows P-833 and P-834;
 harvest rows 1735 to 1741). Put together from main's folder of 2026-11-12, by
 the direction entered as P-832, for main to land after its own check. It
 mends nothing. THE ARC holds main's two tables of every finding word for
 word, its 24 files of checks as it wrote them, a recount of every number from
 the tables, from the outputs main kept and from git, the planted suite's
 output on the commit read, and a lock. The lock runs the recount and three of
 main's four checks of quotations, and holds every other check by hash;
 planted against, it fails on 14 of 14 changes, and the gates on a review's
 entry on 3 of 3. THE ENTRY is in the form of Review 79's. Its anchor is the
 commit the readers read, c40446392. Where the form asks for a judgement that
 main's folder does not give, the entry says so and does not make it: what
 each reader in fact read; the kinds the findings fall into; whether a new
 pair of words needs an entry; promotions; held-out targets. THE LOOP: on
 main's register every row that Review 79's eighteen items name is QUEUED, so
 none is resolved and all eighteen are carried, each with a reason taken from
 its row. Five are at their third carry (R79-5 to R79-9). The rule of
 2026-10-03 asks that each be resolved, declined or waived by the owner; none
 of the three is done here, and the gate does not see it, because it reads
 only lines marked as carried and this block, like Review 79's, restates a
 carried item as open. That is left for main (R80-21). MAIN'S CHECKS WERE MADE
 AGAIN: the three kept checks of quotations, the strict recheck of Review 79's
 and the computation on B1895 give the same bytes; the two sets of plants give
 the same answers. FOUR THINGS GO BACK TO MAIN: one plant of main's own passes
 B1885's lock, where the answer to agy-002's finding 14 says the lock holds
 the note; one check ends in an error after writing its file; one kept output
 has no script in the folder; one recount prints times in the zone of the
 machine and asks for a commit that only main's own repository holds. THE
 LEDGERS: five harvest rows for the four readers' files and the web seat's
 addition, and two more that register by file name, unread, the two deliveries
 that stand before a reader's file on its branch, because the ledger's own
 rule moves a pin to the last commit a row cites; four pins moved; one
 register row, P-834, and the floor of the register's count raised to 834 with
 it; a dated note on P-824 and on P-833. THE PAGES A REVIEW'S LANDING CARRIES:
 the changelog and the log; the status page's newest paragraph; a dated note
 on the five navigation pages that had not been touched since the anchor, each
 saying that the page was not assessed. GENERATED, as a clean checkout makes
 them: four pages of views, the front page's state block, the atlas's data,
 and the page and data of where the programme stands. On this patch every one
 of the 53 gates passes, and the 291 test files that read a page it changes
 give 3,167 passed and 2 failed where main's head gives 3,160 and the same 2.
 The instruments: 24 of 37 planted cases caught on the commit read, 5 of 5
 controls. Tested against planted errors, by the builder of what is tested;
 reproduced, the checks of main's that give the same bytes; computed once; not
 independently checked. 0 of 19.

